# USAGE: Populate this list using `defaults-domains-list` output, and then
#        comment those domains you want `defaults-domains-dump` to report.
# - I.e, commented domain names allowed, everything else blocked.
# - If you cloned this project to ~/.kit/mOS/macOS-GNOME-onboarder, you could run:
#     meld ~/.kit/mOS/macOS-GNOME-onboarder/lib/defaults-domains-block.list \
#       <(defaults-domains-list)
#
# USAGE: Run `bin/slather-defaults.sh --cnt-run` to see list of domains
#        actually used with `defaults` calls, and ensure those exposed
#        (commented) below.

# Note that defaults-domains-dump always captures NSGlobalDomain, aka "Apple Global Domain".

# HSTRY/2025-01-12: Original list from Debian 12:
#   gsettings list-schemas | sed 's/^/# /' | xclip -selection c

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

